{
  "id": "how-cross-team-flag-jobs-iterate-commands-and-temporal-healt",
  "title": "How cross-team flag jobs iterate (commands and Temporal health checks)",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "How do flag management commands iterate over teams?",
    "How does the Temporal health check batch teams?",
    "Where is get_teams_with_flags_queryset?"
  ],
  "body": "- Cache commands (`warm_flags_cache`, `warm_flag_definitions_cache`, `verify_*`) subclass `posthog/management/commands/_base_hypercache_command.py:BaseHyperCacheCommand`; team scope from `flags_cache.py:get_teams_with_flags_queryset` (uses `objects_including_soft_deleted`, teams that ever had a flag); verify chunks of 1000 via `process_teams_in_chunks`; per-team `flags_cache.py:verify_team_flags`, `local_evaluation.py:verify_team_flag_definitions`.\n- `audit_flag_filters` (products/.../management/commands) iterates flags directly by id keyset pagination, 500/page (`_iter_flag_rows`), since PgBouncer disables server-side cursors.\n- Temporal: `posthog/temporal/health_checks/activities.py:_get_team_id_batches_sync` (Team.objects.exclude(id=0), rollout % filter, batch_size chunks) → `workflows.py:HealthCheckWorkflow.run` → `run_health_check_batch` per batch → check's `detect(team_ids)`.\n- `StaleFeatureFlagsCheck.detect` queries FeatureFlag by team_id__in, active, not deleted/archived; weekly cron `0 6 * * 1`, dry_run=True.",
  "tags": [
    "management-commands",
    "temporal",
    "health-checks"
  ],
